// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// rules/tables/ - one table each. Copy this file, rename it, and delete this header.
//
//   Name it  <Table>Rules.cs  and name the class the same: ItemRules.cs holds ItemRules.
//   The part before `Rules` is the table, and the run refuses a name no table has - so a renamed
//   table gets a message rather than a rule that quietly stopped checking.
//
//   Rename to `.cs`. A `.template` file is not scanned, which is the only reason this one can sit
//   here without the run trying to execute it.
//
// When it runs   After the sheets are read and the model is built. These rules run at the same
//                time as each other, so none of them may depend on the order - a rule that has to
//                see several tables at once belongs in rules/global/.
//
// What you get   context.Tables  the accessor generated from the sheets. Every field is typed, so
//                                a misspelling is a compile error rather than a wrong result.
//                                The static `Tables` is the same data reached globally - either
//                                works, and this one is the instance this run loaded.
//                context         ITableContext: how a rule reports. Pass the row and the field
//                                name and the message points at the cell the value came from.
//                context.Table   this table's own schema - its columns, their types, where each
//                                was declared. The file name already says which table, so this
//                                does not repeat it.
//                context.Schema, context.Option(...), context.Files(...), context.Json(...)
//
// Not here       context.Db(...) and context.Redis(...) - those are rules/runtime/ only, and not
//                on this type.
//                [RulePriority] - it is refused here, because there is no order among rules that
//                run at the same time.
//
// This folder is flat. A file one level down is not run at all; put shared helpers in
// rules/shared/.
//
// Full guide: doc/validation.md
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

